%description:

The Binder's X2 peer table (Binder::getX2PeerAddress(), hasX2Peer()):
asking for the X2 address of a base station that is no X2 peer is an error,
named after the missing link, and leaves the table as it was. A base station
sends over X2 to its X2 peers only; a lookup that misses means that the
network lacks the X2 link (e.g. a dual connectivity network whose secondary
node has no X2 client to its master), and the error has to say so, not
leave an unspecified address for the X2 tunnel to fail on later.

Checked with base station 1 having an X2 link to base station 3, and none
to 2; base station 2 has no X2 links at all.

%includes:
#include "SchedulerTestUtil.h"
#include "simu5g/common/binder/Binder.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;

%file: harness.ned
import simu5g.common.binder.Binder;

network Harness
{
    submodules:
        binder: Binder;
        test: Test;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = Harness
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = ""
sim-time-limit = 1s
*.binder.printTrafficGeneratorConfig = false

%no-default-inifile: 1

%activity:
Checker c;
Binder *binder = check_and_cast<Binder *>(getSimulation()->getSystemModule()->getSubmodule("binder"));
const X2NodeId bs1 = MacNodeId(1), bs2 = MacNodeId(2), bs3 = MacNodeId(3);
const inet::L3Address address3(inet::Ipv4Address("10.0.0.3"));
binder->setX2PeerAddress(bs1, bs3, address3);

c.check("the X2 address of a peer is the one set", binder->getX2PeerAddress(bs1, bs3) == address3);

auto lookupThrows = [&] (X2NodeId src, X2NodeId dest, std::string& message) {
    try {
        binder->getX2PeerAddress(src, dest);
        return false;
    }
    catch (cRuntimeError& e) {
        message = e.what();
        return true;
    }
};
std::string message;
c.check("asking for the X2 address of a base station that is no peer is an error",
        lookupThrows(bs1, bs2, message), message);
c.check("...and the error names the missing link",
        message.find("base station 1 has no X2 link to 2") != std::string::npos, message);
message.clear();
c.check("...also for a base station that has no X2 links at all", lookupThrows(bs2, bs1, message), message);
c.check("...and a failed lookup adds no link to the table",
        !binder->hasX2Peer(bs1, bs2) && !binder->hasX2Peer(bs2, bs1) && binder->hasX2Peer(bs1, bs3));

c.summary();

%contains: stdout
modelchecks=5 modelfailures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
